    "passage": "As Christmas is around the corner, you may hear a lot of Christmas songs, including some classics and the album, Everyday is Christmas. This is the eighth studio album and the first Christmas album by the Australian singer-songwriter Sia, who often wears a wig that hides her face to protect her privacy.\nEveryday is Christmas features Christmas songs, released with ten tracks in 2017 [[1]]. Then it was reissued in 2018, 2021, 2022 with extra tracks added each time. You may [[2]] “Santa’s Coming for Us,” “Snowman” and “Candy Cane Lane,” to name a few.\n[[3]] for being changeable and inconsistent, the album is compared to “opening a gift where someone has forgotten to remove the tags.” Besides, some describe the album as “vaguely festive.” However, ABC News praises the record, [[4]] Sia for designing the album for those who are turned off by the so-called holiday classics.\nSia’s voice is considered deep, playful and powerful; some critics even comment that her throaty, slurred vocals can deal with melancholy and obsession. Due to her artistry, she has been nominated for the Grammy Award nine times, and [[5]] the MTV Video Music Award in 2014. She is by all means a distinct singer-songwriter.",
